# Self-hosted cron schedule - mirrors the cloud deployment's split between
# vercel.json (daily-ranks) and .github/workflows (hourly-gsc). Times are
# container-local (UTC). Output is redirected to PID 1's stdout so
# `docker compose logs cron` shows every run (BusyBox crond otherwise
# discards job output).
#
# weekly-opportunities is deliberately NOT scheduled here. The route is
# retired (its own header says so - the Claude weekly-research run replaced
# it) and has no trigger on the cloud deployment, but this crontab kept
# firing it every Monday on self-host only. Three problems, all silent:
# it is hard-scoped to DEFAULT_PROJECT_ID, so on a multi-site install only
# the first site ever got it; it duplicates the research the in-stack
# builder already claims on its own cadence; and it spends the owner's
# DataForSEO balance (keywordIdeas, 200 rows) for an automation that appears
# nowhere in the automations registry and has no toggle to turn off. The
# route stays callable by hand - it just no longer runs behind anyone's back.
0 4 * * * /bin/sh /usr/local/bin/hit.sh daily-ranks >> /proc/1/fd/1 2>&1
7 */3 * * * /bin/sh /usr/local/bin/hit.sh hourly-gsc >> /proc/1/fd/1 2>&1
# Collects the finished DataForSEO standard-queue SERP tasks that daily-ranks
# posts (see dataforseo-tasks.ts) - without this, self-host rank tracking
# would queue tasks that never land. Mirrors .github/workflows/serp-collect.yml.
37 * * * * /bin/sh /usr/local/bin/hit.sh serp-collect >> /proc/1/fd/1 2>&1
# Wakes the SEO workflows in each connected repo when there is work for them,
# replacing the cron chains those workflows used to carry (see
# .github/workflows/seo-dispatch.yml for the full reasoning). On a docker
# install running the in-stack builder this is a no-op by design: the route
# stands down when the builder's heartbeat is fresh, so the two runners can
# never both claim the same job. It matters for the self-host that connected a
# repo but does NOT run the builder container - before this, that install's
# only scheduler was GitHub's own, which is what we are moving away from.
41 */3 * * * /bin/sh /usr/local/bin/hit.sh seo-dispatch >> /proc/1/fd/1 2>&1
